    "title": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "10 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-03 21:20:00 PDT Expires: 2025-09-03 21:45:00 PDT Urgency: Immediate Severity: Severe Certainty: Observed Instruction: For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a building. Target Area: Pinal, AZ SVRPSR\nThe National Weather Service in Phoenix has issued a\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for... Pinal County in southeastern Arizona...\n* Until 945 PM MST.\n* At 920 PM MST, a severe thunderstorm was located near Maricopa, or 12 miles southwest of Sun Lakes, and is nearly stationary.\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n* Locations impacted include... Maricopa, Estrella Sailport, and Ak-Chin Village.\nThis includes the following highways... AZ Route 238 between mile markers 38 and 44. AZ Route 347 between mile markers 170 and 182.",
